  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat a skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "While the skillet heats up, wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 small pkg fresh basil"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add oil and swirl to coat the bottom. Add sausage and cook, breaking the meat apart with a spoon, until browned and crumbly, 3-4 minutes. Transfer cooked sausage to a 4-quart slow cooker insert.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "2 tsp extra virgin olive oil\n1 lb ground pork sausage"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, peel, trim, and medium dice eggplants. Trim off root end and stalks of the fennel, leaving only the white bulbs. Halve fennel bulbs lengthwise, then slice crosswise into thin half-moons. Add both to the slow cooker with the cooked sausage.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Add tomatoes, broth, tomato paste, garlic, and spices to the slow cooker. Stir to combine the sauce, cover, and cook until veggies are tender, 6-7 hours on LOW or 3 hours on HIGH. ",
      "secondary_message": "1 (14.5 oz) can fire-roasted diced tomatoes\n1 ½ cups chicken or vegetable broth\n2 tbsp tomato paste\n1 tbsp minced garlic\n1 tsp Italian seasoning\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp crushed red pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the sauce is done, pick basil leaves off the stems, roll up crosswise, and roughly chop. Add basil and pasta to the slow cooker, then stir to combine. Change slow cooker to high and continue to cook until pasta is tender, about 30 minutes. Remove from heat.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "10 oz penne pasta"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Sprinkle cheese over the pasta in the slow cooker, cover, and let sit until cheese is melted, about 10 minutes.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 cup shredded cheese, Italian blend"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide pasta between plates or bowls and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
